        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='7780' hidden='true' id='20' story-point-id='12' type-v2='text' w='79823' x='1575' y='35685'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#304a66' fontname='Arial Black' fontsize='20' italic='true'>Branches with the Highest Default Loans</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='11411' id='21' story-point-id='14' type-v2='text' w='60138' x='39567' y='48029'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#598abe' fontname='Arial' fontsize='16'>This analysis identifies branches with low recovery percentages and poor loan recovery performance.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='11411' hidden='true' id='22' story-point-id='13' type-v2='text' w='47146' x='34744' y='17116'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#598abe' fontname='Arial' fontsize='16'>Customers are categorized into risk levels based on credit score and loan repayment behavior.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='12863' hidden='true' id='23' story-point-id='12' type-v2='text' w='88287' x='1772' y='41909'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#598abe' fontname='Arial' fontsize='16'>This analysis identifies branches with the highest defaulted loan amounts. It helps detect branches with poor loan repayment performance and higher financial risk exposure.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='56639' hidden='true' id='24' story-point-id='15' type-v2='text' w='90354' x='3150' y='42739'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Data Breakdown &amp; Financial Insights:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The story page displays a summary table with four core financial metrics.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>1. Portfolio Scale</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>total customers : 500</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Insight: The analysis is built on  active portfolio of 500 unique customers. This establishes the baseline for all the aggregated financial figures below.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>2. Total Loan Capital</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Total loan amont: 1,285,933,399 (Approx. 1.29 Billion)</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Insight: This represents the total principal amount disbursed across the 500 customers.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>3. Outstanding Debt</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Remaining Balance: 654,185,945 (Approx. 654.2 Million)</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Insight: This is the total outstanding principal remaining to be collected from the borrowers.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>4. Revenue / Collection Progress</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Total EMI Collected: 32,901,622 (Approx. 32.9 Million)</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Insight: This figure tracks the total Equated Monthly Installments (EMIs) collected so far.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='32158' hidden='true' id='25' story-point-id='2' type-v2='text' w='68012' x='30512' y='30913'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>An analysis of the total loan amount reveals a diversified portfolio with no single dominant category.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Top Contributor: </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Car Loans </run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>lead the portfolio at </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>28,21,22,180 (approx. 22% of total).</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Core Middle: Education Loans (26.72M), Home Loans (26.24M), and Personal Loans (25.49M) follow in tight succession, each representing roughly 20% of the total.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Lowest Contributor: Business Loans bring in the lowest total at 21,91,17,970 (approx. 17%), showing room for potential commercial growth.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='34647' hidden='true' id='26' story-point-id='3' type-v2='text' w='70866' x='8465' y='63174'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Maximum Approvals: 48</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Minimum Approvals: 33</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Ending Volume: 45</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The operational trend in this chart shows a fluctuating demand curve with a 45% variance between the lowest month (33) and the highest peak (48). This pattern suggests that external seasonal factors or marketing campaigns may heavily influence loan applications. Investigating the operational bottlenecks during the drop to 33, and replicating the success strategies of the 47 and 48 approval peaks, will help stabilize monthly revenue streams.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='17635' hidden='true' id='27' story-point-id='4' type-v2='text' w='99508' x='394' y='82676'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>An analysis of the data reveals a highly competitive ceiling for individual loan allocations:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Peak:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'> Jiya Bhalla holds the single largest individual loan amount at 49,81,738, followed marginally by Shanaya Saha (49,76,503) and Kashvi Chauhan (49,72,643).</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Cluster</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>: The remaining seven high-value clients—including Tara Dash, Seher Mane, and Jayan Venkatesh—all sit tightly above the 49.2M mark.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>T</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>he Threshold</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>: Shray Arya rounds out the top ten list at 49,08,278, establishing a clear ~49L benchmark required to break into the organization&apos;s top tier of individual borrowers.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='15353' hidden='true' id='28' story-point-id='4' type-v2='text' w='25492' x='74311' y='62759'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='11'>Key Metrics Checklist:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='11'>Top Borrower: Jiya Bhalla (49,81,738)</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='11'>#2 Borrower: Shanaya Saha (49,76,503)</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='24689' hidden='true' id='29' story-point-id='5' type-v2='text' w='98130' x='2264' y='80187'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Key Metrics Checklist:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Top State: </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Semibold' fontsize='10'>Maharashtra (27,59,92,497)</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Runner-Up State: </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Semibold' fontsize='10'>Punjab (15,69,66,392)</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Lowest Visible State: </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Semibold' fontsize='10'>Kerala (9,59,95,974)</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Primary Market:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'> Maharashtra is the undisputed leader with 27,59,92,497, anchoring the largest share of the portfolio.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Mid-Tier Cluster</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>: A secondary tier of states is tightly grouped between 12M and 16M, led by Punjab (15.69M), followed closely by Uttar Pradesh (13.69M), Delhi (13.28M), Rajasthan (12.58M), Telangana (12.49M), and Bihar (12.18M).</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Lower Tier:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'> West Bengal (11.45M) and Kerala (9.59M) constitute the lowest loan volumes among the visible states, pointing to potential areas for regional expansion.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='24066' hidden='true' id='30' story-point-id='6' type-v2='text' w='33858' x='66043' y='63900'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Key Metrics Checklist:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Card: 26.70% (Highest)</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Bank Transfer: 25.14%</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>UPI: 24.73%</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Cash: 23.43% (Lowest)</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Total Variance: Only 3.27% separating the top mode from the bottom.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='35996' hidden='true' id='31' story-point-id='12' type-v2='text' w='90846' x='1673' y='53734'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Risk Distribution Highlights High Discrepancy Across Top Defaulting Branches</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The data in visual  maps out the core centers of poor loan repayment performance:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Highest Risk Sector: </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='11'>Jaipur Finance Branch leads</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'> the chart with a notable </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='12'>23.415% share</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>of the default amount.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Secondary Tier:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='12'>Lucknow Finance Branch</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'> also shows elevated exposure, </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='12'>accounting for 20.209%.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Stable Cluster</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>: The baseline of this high-default group features </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='12'>Hyderabad (18.983%), Pune (18.700%),</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'> and a secondary</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='12'> Hyderabad entity (18.693%)</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>, showing near-identical risk volumes.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='39212' hidden='true' id='32' story-point-id='13' type-v2='text' w='63976' x='34744' y='28631'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The distribution data in chart  highlights how customers segment across established credit brackets:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Primary Group (Highest Volume):</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'> The first risk bracket holds the largest share of the portfolio with </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='12'>263 customers.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Secondary Group (Moderate Volume)</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>: The second bracket maintains a strong presence with </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='12'>200 customers.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Outlier (Lowest Volume):</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'> The final tier sees a massive drop-off, accounting for only</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='12'> 37 customers</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>—roughly 7.4% of the total customer pool analyzed.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='41390' id='33' story-point-id='14' type-v2='text' w='58760' x='40059' y='58299'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>Performance Breakdown of Bottom-Tier Loan Recovery Channels</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The comparative chart  details the organization&apos;s lowest recovery brackets:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Absolute Lowest</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>: The worst-performing branch flags a critical </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Semibold' fontsize='10'>14.76%</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'> recovery rate.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Mid-Low Tier:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'> The next branch shows slight improvement but remains highly vulnerable at </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Semibold' fontsize='10'>16.54%.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The Upper-Low Cluster: </run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='10'>The final three underperforming branches cluster tightly together, posting closely grouped recovery rates of </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Semibold' fontsize='10'>17.77%, 18.00%, and 18.39%.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{F9DC1CAD-919F-426C-9478-B9C78EA0EECA}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
